{"r":"rgb","lane":{"p":1110,"e":[{"h":"رَغِبَ","t":["aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"رَغْبَةٌ"]," (JK, TA) and ",[2,"رَغْبَى"]," (JK) [and app. ",[2,"رَغَبٌ"]," &c. as in the next sentence but one], ",[1,"He desired a thing"]," [app. in an absolute sense, agreeably with what follows in the next sentence but one: and also,] ",[1,"vehemently, eagerly, greedily, very greedily, with avidity, excessively,"]," or ",[1,"culpably; he coveted a thing, longed for it,"]," or ",[1,"lusted after it."]," (TA.) ",[2,"رَغَبُ النَّفْسِ"]," means ",[1,"The"]," [",[1,"soul's"],"] ",[1,"hoping largely, and desiring much."]," (TA.) ― -b2- ",[2,"رَغِبَ فِيهِ"],", (S, A, Mgh, Msb, K, &c.,) and ",[2,"رَغِبَهُ"],", (Msb, TA,) aor. , (K, TA,) inf. n. ",[2,"رَغْبَةٌ"]," (S, A, * Mgh, K) and ",[2,"رَغَبٌ"]," (S, Msb) and ",[2,"رَغْبٌ"]," (Mgh, Msb, K) and ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"]," (K) and ",[2,"رُغْبَى"]," (A, * Msb) and ",[2,"رَغْبَى"]," (Msb) and ",[2,"رَغْبَآءُ"],", (A, * Msb,) ",[1,"He desired it,"]," or ",[1,"wished for it;"]," (S, A, Mgh, Msb, K;) as also ",[2,"فيه"]," ↓ ",[2,"ارتغب"],". (S, K.) You say, ",[2,"مَا لِى فِيهِ رَغْبَةٌ"]," and ",[2,"رُغْبَى"]," and ",[2,"رَغْبَآءُ"]," [",[1,"I have not any desire,"]," or ",[1,"wish, for it"],"]. (A.) And ",[2,"رُهْبَاكَ خَيْرٌ مِنْ رُغْبَاكَ"],", i. e. ",[1,"The fearing thee is better than the loving thee;"],[2,"رهباك"]," being an inf. n. prefixed to an objective complement; and so ",[2,"رغباك"],": and said to mean, thy being given a thing through fear of thee is better than through desire: a prov., similar to ",[2,"رَهَبُوتٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ رَحَمُوتٍ"],". (Meyd. [Freytag explains it otherwise: see his Arab. Prov. i. 542.]) ― -b3- ",[2,"رَغِبَ عَنْهُ"],[1,"He did not desire it,"]," or ",[1,"wish for it;"]," (S, A, Mgh, Msb, K;) ",[1,"he shunned,"]," or ",[1,"avoided, it; abstained from it;"]," (S, TA;) or ",[1,"left it, relinquished it,"]," or ",[1,"forsook it,"]," (JK, S, TA,) ",[1,"intentionally."]," (JK, TA.) ― -b4- ",[2,"رَغِبَ"],[2,"إِلَيْهِ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"رَغَبٌ"]," (K) and ",[2,"رَغْبٌ"]," and ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"]," (TA) and ",[2,"رُغْبَى"]," (Mgh, * K) and ",[2,"رَغْبَى"]," (K) and ",[2,"رَغْبَآءُ"]," (A, * K) and ",[2,"رَغْبَةٌ"]," (Mgh, * TA) and ",[2,"رُغْبَةٌ"]," and ",[2,"رَغَبَةٌ"]," and ",[2,"رَغَبُوتٌ"],", and ",[2,"رَغَبُوتَى"]," and ",[2,"رَغَبَانٌ"],", (K,) ",[1,"He made petition to him, addressed a petition to him, asked him, petitioned him, sought of him,"]," or ",[1,"demanded of him:"]," (TA:) or ",[1,"he prayed to him,"]," or ",[1,"supplicated him, with humility"]," or ",[1,"abasement,"]," or ",[1,"with sincerity"]," or ",[1,"earnestness"]," or ",[1,"energy:"]," or ",[1,"he humbled,"]," or ",[1,"abased, himself, and made petition to him."]," (K, A, TA.) You say, ",[2,"رَغِبَ إِلَى فُلَانٍ فِى كَذَا"],[1,"He made petition to such a one, petitioned him,"]," or ",[1,"asked him, for such a thing."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"إِلَى"],[2,"ٱللّٰهِ أَرْغَبُ"],[1,"To God I humble,"]," or ",[1,"abase, myself, and make petition;"]," syn. ",[2,"أَضْرَعُ"],": and ",[2,"إِلَيْهش أَرْفَعُ رَغْبَتِى"]," [",[1,"To Him I raise my humble petition"],"]. (A.) And ",[2,"الرُّهْبَى مِنَ ٱللّٰهِ وَالرُّغْبَى إِلَيْهِ"]," [",[1,"Fear"]," should be ",[1,"of God;"]," (not of a creature;) ",[1,"and petition,"]," &c., should be ",[1,"to Him"],"]. (Lth, TA in art. ",[2,"رهب"],".) See also another ex. in a verse cited voce ",[2,"رَغِيبَةٌ"],". ― -b5- ",[2,"رَغِبَ بِنَفْسِهِ عَنْهُ"]," [lit. ",[1,"He made himself to be not desirous of,"]," or ",[1,"to shun,"]," or ",[1,"abstain from,"]," or ",[1,"leave, him,"]," or ",[1,"it;"]," the ",[2,"ب"]," having the same effect as in ",[2,"ذَهَبَ بِهِ"]," &c.; and hence,] ",[1,"he held himself above,"]," or ",[1,"superior to, him,"]," or ",[1,"it."]," (K.) And ",[2,"رَغِبْتُ"],[2,"بِفُلَانٍ عَنْ هٰذَا"],[1,"I made such a one to shun, abstain from,"]," or ",[1,"leave, this, disliking it for him."]," (MF.) -A2- ",[2,"رَغُبَ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"It"]," (anything) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, wide,"]," or ",[1,"ample."]," (TA. [See also 6.]) You say, ",[2,"رَغُبَ"],[2,"الوَادِى"],", aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"]," and ",[2,"رُغُبٌ"]," (K) and ",[2,"رَغَابَةٌ"],", (TA,) (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The valley was large and wide, taking,"]," or ",[1,"receiving, much water."]," (K, * TA.) And ",[2,"رَغُبَتِ الأَرْضُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"]," [&c.], (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The land was soft"]," (S, TA) ",[1,"and wide, with even,"]," or ",[1,"sandy, soil:"]," (TA:) or (S, TA) ",[1,"took much water;"]," (TA;) ",[1,"was such as would not flow unless in consequence of much rain."]," (S, TA.) ― -b2- And [hence,] ",[2,"رَغُبَ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"]," (S, K *) and ",[2,"رُغُبٌ"],", (K, * TA,) (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, voracious, a great eater;"]," (K, TA;) ",[1,"very greedy,"]," or ",[1,"gluttonous;"]," (S, K, TA;) ",[1,"vehemently, excessively,"]," or ",[1,"culpably, desirous of worldly goods, and one who made himself to be large,"]," or ",[1,"abundant, therein:"]," or as some say, ",[1,"large in his hopes,"],[1,"and desirous of much."]," (TA.) Accord. to the T, ",[2,"رُغْبُ البَطْنِ"]," signifies (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Voracity:"]," and ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"],", alone, as occurring in a trad., is explained as meaning ",[1,"capaciousness of the belly, and voracity."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"رَغُبَ رَأْيُهُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"رُغْبٌ"],", (tropical:) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, liberal,"]," or ",[1,"bountiful, and large in opinion"]," or ",[1,"judgment."]," (A.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"رغّبهُ فِى شَىْءٍ","t":["[inf. n. ",[2,"تَرْغِيبٌ"],",] ",[1,"He made him to desire,"]," or ",[1,"wish for, a thing;"]," (S, * MA, K; *) as also ",[2,"فيه"]," ↓ ",[2,"ارغبهُ"],". (S, * K: *) both signify the same. (S.) You say, ",[2,"رَغَّبْتُهُ فِى صُحْبَتِهِ"]," [",[1,"I made him to desire,"]," or ",[1,"wish for, his companionship"],"]. (A.) ― -b2- And ",[2,"رغّبهُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"تَرْغِيبٌ"],"; (IAar, TA;) and ",[2,"رغّب إِلَيْهِ"],"; (TA;) ",[1,"He gave